                ]
            },
            "value": {
                "none": [
                    "Summer is coming to a close on Long Island, and Alex is no longer welcome.\n\nA misstep at a dinner party, and the older man she's been staying with dismisses her with a ride to the train station and a ticket back to the city.\n\nWith few resources and a waterlogged phone, but gifted with an ability to navigate the desires of others, Alex stays on Long Island and drifts like a ghost through the hedged lanes, gated driveways and sun-blasted dunes of a rarified world that is, at first, closed to her. Propelled by desperation and a mutable sense of morality, she spends the week leading up to the end of the holidays moving from one place to the next, a cipher leaving destruction in her wake."
                ]
